assistant: Subject: send an Idempotency-Key when creating orders

Vendor version 2026-10-01 still answers `POST /orders` with a 200 and an order id, but it seems to no longer save orders placed without an `Idempotency-Key` header. The spec has always listed that header as recommended, and shop-mcp never sent it, so `GET /orders/o-5002` returned 404 right after the create. I couldn't run the live vendor, so this cause is inferred, not confirmed: the header is the only thing the spec says the client can change on this request. The fix is in `src/tools/create_order.ts`: `create_order` now sends a new random UUID as the `Idempotency-Key` on every call, so each new order gets its own key and none is reused. Typecheck and lint pass, and so does every test except two, as the rules expect: the repro test and the v1 `order-create.json` fixture both report UNMATCHED_REQUEST because their recordings don't have the new header. They need re-recording, and the v1 output should stay the same because v1 accepts this optional header. I left one other change alone because it's outside this fix: 2026-10-01 now returns `created_at` as epoch milliseconds, and `get_order` doesn't parse that format yet.

Subject: send an Idempotency-Key when creating orders

